      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://qy-feng.github.io/authors/admin/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Qianyu Feng is a second-year Ph.D. student at &lt;a href=&#34;http://reler.net/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;ReLER Lab&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.uts.edu.au/research-and-teaching/our-research/centre-artificial-intelligence&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Australian Artificial Intelligence Institute (AAII)&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.uts.edu.au/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;University of Technology Sydney (UTS)&lt;/a&gt;. Her academic advisors are &lt;a href=&#34;https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=RMSuNFwAAAAJ&amp;amp;hl=en&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Prof. Yi Yang&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=vNHqr3oAAAAJ&amp;amp;hl=en&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Prof. Liang Zheng&lt;/a&gt;. Her research interests include cross-domain representation learning and linguistic-vision applications. She speaks fluent in multiple languages, including Chinese, English and French. She is an advocator and member of &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.uts.edu.au/about/faculty-engineering-and-information-technology/women-engineering-and-it&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Women in Engineering and IT&lt;/a&gt;. She is building AI systems aligning &lt;strong&gt;human-centred values&lt;/strong&gt; and ensuring the &lt;strong&gt;fairness, reliability and accountability&lt;/strong&gt; throughout their lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artificial Intelligence Is Too Important to Leave to Men Alone&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
</description>
